<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13530] Java thin: exception type is lost on rethrow</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13530</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Exception handling in TcpClientChannel is inconsistent:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Some code is duplicated in &lt;tt&gt;receive&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;convertException&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Some exception types, like &lt;tt&gt;ClientAuthenticationException&lt;/tt&gt;, are wrapped in &lt;tt&gt;ClientException&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Make sure to preserve exception types when rethrowing them and deduplicate the code.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
